{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:6f287d8260368a8103b8bee1a60e3f6f", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 12, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Both steps are done. Summary:\n\n1. **`migrate.sql`** - Added the missing `loyalty` column to `customers` (`ALTER TABLE customers ADD COLUMN loyalty TEXT;`), then backfilled it from `legacy_code` using a `CASE` statement with the mapping from `codes.csv` (A→gold, B→silver, C→bronze). Rows with unrecognized codes are left with `NULL` rather than being silently mapped to a wrong tier.\n\n2. **`./run-migration.sh`** - Ran successfully (exit 0); it applied the migration to the staging database as its script does.", "turn_key": "sha256:097eb3966f9220b032e453e5cca297b3"}
